# (build 160) A rebind end to end: START's KEY 1 set to Q on the CONTROLS
# page, DOWN's 1ST to the right stick down on the BUTTONS page, then each
# raw press made what the platform makes of it through the menu's
# controls (`key`, `pad`): on the title Enter, the old Start key, does
# nothing and Q leaves it; on NEW GAME / CONTINUE the d-pad down, the old
# down, does nothing and the right stick down moves the cursor, as the
# down arrow (DOWN's KEY 1, unchanged) still does. tools/controls_check.py
# does the same through the headless game, its platform and settings.json.

start new
wait screen title
press esc
press down                   # CONTROLS
press c
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down                   # START
press c
key Q
expect keys start Q / -
press b                      # the menu, on CONTROLS
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down                   # GAMEPAD
press c
press down
press down
press down                   # BUTTONS
press c
press down                   # DOWN
press c
pad RSDOWN
expect buttons down RS DOWN / LS DOWN
press b                      # the GAMEPAD page
press b                      # the menu
press b
expect escape-menu closed

expect screen title
key RETURN                   # Start no more
wait ticks 20
expect screen title
key Q                        # Start now
wait screen intro
wait idle
expect menu $37 0            # NEW GAME
pad DDOWN                    # down no more
wait ticks 10
expect menu $37 0
pad RSDOWN                   # down now
wait idle
expect menu $37 1            # CONTINUE
key DOWN                     # the arrow, still down
wait idle
expect menu $37 2            # ERASE GAME
shot 01_moved
